        {
          "id": 1209092484,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Yes, if you use `dissector_try_payload_new()` you can pass data with a payload table (the second Decode As table you set up here) the same as a uint table.\n\nIt might make sense to make the first uint table based on the proto Decode As too. I know there's code in `packet-gfp.c` that demonstrates how to do that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
